21
00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:25.860
Because economists forgot to include the dying part. For centuries, economics measured productivity without accounting for

22
00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.420
the people who stopped being productive on account of being dead.

23
00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:36.160
This is like calculating the cost of a plane crash without including the plane, the passengers, or the fact that they were

24
00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:41.820
going somewhere. The Actual Bill (Economist-Approved Misery Accounting).

25
00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:51.040
Here's what disease actually costs, translated from economist-speak into human language: Direct Medical Costs mean paying

26
00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:59.020
doctors to Google your symptoms in a room that costs five hundred dollars per hour, at an annual cost of eight point two

27
00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:07.640
trillion dollars. Lost Productivity means sick people make fewer spreadsheets, decreasing global PowerPoint supply, at an

28
00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:17.120
