29
00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:25.880
dead people contribute zero to the economy (economists finally noticed), at an annual cost of three hundred eighty-two point

30
00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:36.440
five trillion dollars. The TOTAL DISASTER is more money than exists on Earth, for an annual total of three hundred ninety-seven

31
00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:43.740
point four trillion dollars. Let me explain that last one, because it's where the real horror lives.

32
00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:48.460
How to Measure Suffering Without Feeling Feelings (The D.A.L.Y.).

33
00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:56.900
disability-adjusted life years, or D.A.L.Y. stands for "Disability-Adjusted Life Year."

34
00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:02.970
That's economist-speak for "quantifying human misery without having to look people in the eye.".

35
00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:08.060
One D.A.L.Y. equals One year of healthy human life, deleted.

36
00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:15.220
Die at 40 instead of 80? That's 40 D.A.L.Y.s. Spend 10 years severely depressed?

37
00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:24.100
That's 5 D.A.L.Y.s (economists calculated that being miserable counts as being half-dead, which is oddly accurate).

38
00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:31.920
The entire human species combined? 2.55 BILLION D.A.L.Y.s annually.

39
00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:41.380
That's two point five five billion years of human potential, dissolving annually into medical bills and funeral expenses.

40
00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:51.560
What the W.H.O. Thinks You're Worth (Less Than a Tesla). The World Health Organization decided one year of human life is

41
00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:58.540
worth one to three times G.D.P. per capita. They made this calculation sober, which is surprising.

42
00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:07.320
Let's use three times G.D.P. per capita. We're optimists who think humans are worth at least three years of their economic

43
00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:14.140
